X86 seqlock-recheck-vs-payload-x86-RELAXED-control
(*
 * THE CONCEALMENT, FOR PAIR (b). Byte-for-byte the same defective reader as
 * `seqlock-recheck-vs-payload-aarch64-RELAXED-control.litmus`, which is
 * ALLOWED.
 *
 * RESULT (herd7 7.58, 2026-08-24): **FORBIDDEN / "Never"**.
 *
 * A seqlock reader missing its acquire fence is CORRECT on x86-TSO and WRONG on
 * ARMv8. This is why MV3's gate demands a verdict per memory model: one summary
 * verdict over these three files would read "Sometimes" and say nothing about
 * WHERE, and a summary verdict over M3's lost-wakeup pair concealed the mirror
 * image of exactly this.
 *)
{ seq=0; d1=0; d2=0; }
 P0                 | P1                 ;
 MOV [seq],$1       | MOV EAX,[seq]      ;
 MOV [d1],$1        | MOV EBX,[d1]       ;
 MOV [d2],$1        | MOV ECX,[d2]       ;
 MOV [seq],$2       | MOV EDX,[seq]      ;
exists (1:EAX=0 /\ 1:EDX=0 /\ (1:EBX=1 \/ 1:ECX=1))
